Here is a more complete answer to your original question, assuming you are asking about how to scrape data from a website using Jsoup in Java:

```java
import org.jsoup.Jsoup;
import org.jsoup.nodes.Document;
import org.jsoup.nodes.Element;
import org.jsoup.select.Elements;

public class WebScraper {

    public static String url = "http://www.example.com";

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Document document = sendGetRequest(url);
        
        // Get the title of the webpage
        Element titleElement = document.select("title").first();
        if (titleElement != null) {
            System.out.println("Title: " + titleElement.text());
        } else {
            System.out.println("No title found.");
        }

        // Get all links on the webpage
        Elements links = document.select("a");
        for (Element link : links) {
            System.out.println(link.attr("href"));
        }

        // Get all paragraph elements on the webpage
        Elements paragraphs = document.select("p");
        for (Element paragraph : paragraphs) {
            System.out.println(paragraph.text());
        }
    }

    public static Document sendGetRequest(String url) {
        return Jsoup.connect(url).get();
    }
}
```

In this example, we're using Jsoup to connect to the provided URL and retrieve its HTML content. We then use various methods (like `select()` and `attr()`) to extract specific data from the HTML.

Please note that you should always respect the website's terms of service when web scraping.
