Here is a complete solution to scrape data from a website using Jsoup in Java, assuming you want to extract all paragraphs and links from a webpage:

```java
import org.jsoup.Jsoup;
import org.jsoup.nodes.Document;
import org.jsoup.nodes.Element;
import org.jsoup.select.Elements;

public class WebScraper {

    public static String url = "http://www.example.com";

    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Document document = sendGetRequest(url);
        
        // Get all paragraphs on the webpage
        Elements paragraphs = document.select("p");
        if (paragraphs != null && !paragraphs.isEmpty()) {
            for (Element paragraph : paragraphs) {
                System.out.println(paragraph.text());
            }
        } else {
            System.out.println("No paragraphs found.");
        }

        // Get all links on the webpage
        Elements links = document.select("a");
        if (links != null && !links.isEmpty()) {
            for (Element link : links) {
                System.out.println(link.attr("href"));
            }
        } else {
            System.out.println("No links found.");
        }
    }

    public static Document sendGetRequest(String url) {
        return Jsoup.connect(url).get();
    }
}
```

In this example, we're using Jsoup to connect to the provided URL and retrieve its HTML content. We then use the `select()` method to extract all paragraphs (`<p>`) and links (`<a>`) from the HTML.

Please note that you should always respect the website's terms of service when web scraping. Also, be aware that some websites may block or limit your requests if they detect excessive scraping activity.

Also, please make sure to replace `"http://www.example.com"` with the actual URL you want to scrape.

If you have any specific requirements or questions, feel free to ask!
